# Written only when a project has none of its own; a project's .dockerignore
# is left exactly as the customer wrote it.
#
# .git is the load-bearing line. Two clones of one repository give an
# identical worktree and different .git bytes, so leaving it in the build
# context made `COPY . .` hash differently on every deploy and rebuilt every
# layer below it. See DockerIgnore for the measurement.
.git
node_modules
.panelalpha
npm-debug.log

# The engine's own generated files. They are regenerated every deploy and they
# live in the build context, so any change to them -- a new port, a changed
# URL -- rebuilt every layer from `COPY . .` down. Nothing inside the image
# reads either of them. panelalpha-entrypoint.sh is NOT here: the Dockerfile
# copies it by name.
panelalpha.Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
